WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.279
I can't tell you right now what things are
going to be like in November.

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.000
I can only tell you what things are like right
now.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.200
And right now, Donald Trump and Joe Biden
are.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:19.600
Seeing a shift in who is supporting them and
older voters are abandoning Donald Trump and

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.150
they are flocking to Joe Biden in large numbers.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.520
Why do we care while we care about every vote?

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.920
But in particular, we care because older voters
are a key voting group for Donald Trump.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:36.660
If you look back at the 2016 exit polls, Trump
won voters age 50 or older by the largest

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.000
margin.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.870
Trump won voter voters in their 40s by a little
bit, and Trump lost all age groups from thirty

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.440
nine and under.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.630
Republicans in general have done better with
older voters than younger voters for a very

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.630
long time.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.579
So the important thing is Trump needs older
voters to win in November.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:01:01.899
Back in 2016, Trump won voters aged 45 to
64 by 4 percent.

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:08.909
Right now, we've seen a five point swing with
Biden leading that group 45 to 64 by about

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:10.149
one and a half points.

00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:14.149
That's a five and a half point reversal from
2016.

00:01:14.149 --> 00:01:15.689
Normal caveats.

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:16.689
It's early.

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:21.869
A lot can change when we look at voters 65
plus.

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:26.649
Trump won that group by 13 points in 2016.

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:31.790
He is now losing 65 plus by one point to Biden.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.459
That is a 14 point swing.

00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:36.929
Now, why is this happening?

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.039
Speculation.

00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:39.679
It's speculation right now.

00:01:39.679 --> 00:01:44.159
Someone wrote to me and said, David, older
folks are dying from Corona virus and it's

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:48.539
the Trump older folks that are more likely
to die because they're not wearing masks or

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:49.840
staying home.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.689
I understand the logic of that.

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:52.689
It's been floated.

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:54.920
We don't have any evidence for that right
now.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.710
Corona virus in general is the most sort of
obvious explanation.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:05.549
Older folks are most at risk from Corona virus
and they might react the most strongly to

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:07.569
Donald Trump's mishandling of it.

00:02:07.569 --> 00:02:12.430
This problem with older voters that Trump
is having could explain why Trump is not doing

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:15.060
well in states with older populations.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.530
Florida is one such state that's a key state.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.670
Florida's population is the fifth oldest in
the country.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:25.510
The latest polls have Trump losing to Biden
by 6 in Florida.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:32.769
More importantly for today's story, Quinnipiac
has Trump losing by 10 in Florida among voters

00:02:32.769 --> 00:02:34.660
65 and older.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.260
So I don't want to get anybody's hopes up.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.430
We've got to count every vote.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.340
This is a snapshot right now.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.991
But if Trump loses older voters in Florida
by anything close to 10, even by 6 or 7, it's

00:02:45.991 --> 00:02:47.420
over for Trump.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:52.200
Now, if coronavirus starts to wane, if the
economy recovers or appears to recover and

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.030
Trump can attach his name to the recovery,
things could turn around very quickly.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:01.319
So, you know, when you start slicing and dicing
the electorate in this way, it's really difficult

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:03.980
to glean anything super useful from it.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.819
What I do think is interesting is the following.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:13.599
We believe that about 13 percent of people
who voted for Obama-Biden and 26 in 2012 voted

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:14.599
for Trump.

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:21.230
In 2016, 13 percent of Obama's twelve voters
went for Trump in 16.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:29.370
If Biden can get back just half of those people
and not lose anybody that voted for Hillary.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:35.700
That translates to a 7 million vote victory
in the popular vote for Biden in 2020.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:40.719
Now, you could win the popular vote by 7 million
and lose the Electoral College.

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:43.129
It's theoretically possible.

00:03:43.129 --> 00:03:44.129
We've never seen it.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:45.129
We've never seen it.

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:51.340
So now go back and think people who were on
board with Obama in 2012 and voted Trump for

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.719
some reason in 2016.

00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:58.770
Are they likely to stick with Trump over a
guy they already voted for years prior and

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.989
Joe and Joe Biden, if he only gets half of
them back?

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:05.489
It looks very good for Biden.

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:08.090
Again, nothing is guaranteed.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:15.700
If Biden can win back just half of those voters
who went from Obama in 12 to Trump in 16,

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.440
he has a very, very good starting point for
2020.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.530
So what does this mean for us?

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:21.690
Nothing.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.600
All it means is every single one of us needs
to vote.

